<title>USA: Cyclone Drena moving southeast, weakening  - WSC.</title>
<headline>Cyclone Drena moving southeast, weakening  - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Drena, now in the Tasman Sea, will continue moving southeast, weakening and becoming extratropical within 24 hours, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Friday.</p>
<p>Drena has 50 mph winds and is near 35s/170e, moving at 20 mph. The cyclone is only a threat to shipping.</p>
